306 - Draw Me Nearer
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 306
Topic: Gospel - 

Verse 1:
[C]I am Thine, [G/D]O Lord, I have heard [D7]thy [G]voice,
[G]And it told [D7]Thy love to [G]me;
[G/B]But I long [C]to rise in the arms of [G]faith
[G]And be closer [D7]drawn to [G]Thee.

Refrain:
[G]Draw me nearer, [Am]nearer, [D7]blessed [G]Lord,
[G]to the cross where [C]thou hast died.
[G/B]Draw me nearer, [C]nearer, [D7/A]nearer, [G]blessed [D]Lord,
[G]to thy precious, [C]bleeding side.

Verse 2:
[C]Consecrate [G/D]me now to thy service, Lord,
[G]by the power [D7]of grace divine;
[G/B]let my soul [C]look up with a steadfast [G]hope,
[G]and my will [D7]be lost in [G]thine.

Verse 3:
[C]O the pure [G/D]delight of a single hour
[G]that before [D7]thy throne I [G]spend,
[G/B]when I kneel [C]in prayer, and with thee, my [G]God,
[G]I commune [D7]as friend with [G]friend!
